<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17590" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϋτέω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i> pers. impf., and in Trag. (never in <i><span class="en">
			S.
		</span></i>) only in pres. and impf.: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠΰτησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					11.185
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				995.7
			</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔω</span>
				B):—<i>cry, shout,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακρὸν ἀΰτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.50
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ μέγ᾽ ἀΰτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.582
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κληδὼν ἀϋτεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					927
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοιαῦτ᾽ ἀϋτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					384
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΰτει δ᾽ ὀξύ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					1058
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					757
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.
			pers., <i>call to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΰτει πάντας ἀρίστους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.258
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΰτευν Ἄρτεμιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					167
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί Ζῆν᾽ ἀϋτεῖς;</span>
			why <i>call on</i> Zeus? <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				717
			</span></i>: c. acc. pers. et inf., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				668
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. acc. rei,
				<i>call for,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοὰν ἀ.</span>
			<i>call for</i> help, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1092
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>proclaim,</i> c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				4.39
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				428
			</span></i>.</div>
